{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/950771-seers-as-written","id":950771,"title":"Seers As Written","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-14T15:30:38-07:00","id":950771,"title":"Seers As Written","content":"So I just read back through a bunch of threads about tweaking the Seers or making alternate Seers and so forth, and felt the need to explore this in a separate thread instead of hijacking one.<br /> <br /> What have people done that they really enjoyed with the normal version of the Seers? Anything that's been fun to emphasize or play down? <br /> <br /> I'm thinking about ways to play up these shiny cryptofascists as a main set of antagonists in a game and fishing for ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1134-nicias","name":"Nicias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T15:36:27-07:00","id":950773,"title":"","content":"As someone who's always struggled with faith, the idea of achieving Prelacy and having communication with the closest thing the Fallen World has to gods is a potent motivation. <br /> <br /> Beyond that, there's the sheer scale of the threat the Exarchs pose; they won so hard the timeline was forever changed, and trying to struggle against incarnate symbols of oppression is so unthinkably beyond the scope of possibility that it seems hopeless. Why not join the winning team and benefit from it? Why try to change the world if no one's managed a single measurable victory against them ever?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 08-14-2016, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T15:44:55-07:00","id":950774,"title":"","content":"Life as a mage is hard. Unless you're a Seer. Then it's Just that easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T16:20:37-07:00","id":950781,"title":"","content":"So I've recently been talking about this elsewhere, and something I think is really key to emphasize about the Seers of the Throne is their view on magic - &quot;Magic is Payment.&quot; Now contrast that with the Silver Ladder, who are said to be a large part of the driving force behind the Diamond Orders (or at the very least, like to see themselves that way). &quot;Magic is Humanity's Birthright.&quot; It's been said before that Mages are a metaphor for the 1%. Well, if that's the case, then the diamond are the trust fund kids, and the Seers are the business tycoons. From the Seers perspective, they <i>work</i> for their magic. They <i>earned</i> everything they have by getting a job at the Pyramid and working their asses off to impress the Exarchs. What did those Diamond Mages do to deserve their power? Nothing. they were just born into it. And don't even get me started on those socialist Libertines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T16:26:02-07:00","id":950783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/950771-seers-as-written?p=950774#post950774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Life as a mage is hard. Unless you're a Seer. Then it's Just that easy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ... if you don't have morality problems, that is. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T16:30:21-07:00","id":950786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/950771-seers-as-written?p=950781#post950781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I've recently been talking about this elsewhere, and something I think is really key to emphasize about the Seers of the Throne is their view on magic - &quot;Magic is Payment.&quot; Now contrast that with the Silver Ladder, who are said to be a large part of the driving force behind the Diamond Orders (or at the very least, like to see themselves that way). &quot;Magic is Humanity's Birthright.&quot; It's been said before that Mages are a metaphor for the 1%. Well, if that's the case, then the diamond are the trust fund kids, and the Seers are the business tycoons. From the Seers perspective, they <i>work</i> for their magic. They <i>earned</i> everything they have by getting a job at the Pyramid and working their asses off to impress the Exarchs. What did those Diamond Mages do to deserve their power? Nothing. they were just born into it. And don't even get me started on those socialist Libertines.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's an interesting point of view... but they Awoke, just like everyone else, and did it <i>for themselves</i>. The Exarchs wouldn't want another Mage on the surface of the World, but they keep Awakening just the same. If the Diamond ones are the privileged part of the deal, how their continuous existence despirte fighting the very rulers of the cosmos stand?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T16:43:57-07:00","id":950791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/950771-seers-as-written?p=950786#post950786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's an interesting point of view... but they Awoke, just like everyone else, and did it <i>for themselves</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did they, though? Or was it just a handout from those upstart Oracles?*<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/950771-seers-as-written?p=950786#post950786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Exarchs wouldn't want another Mage on the surface of the World, but they keep Awakening just the same. If the Diamond ones are the privileged part of the deal, how their continuous existence despirte fighting the very rulers of the cosmos stand?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's their birthright as humans, isn't it? That's what the Ladder would have you believe, anyway. It's not a paycheck they worked for, it's a privilege they believe themselves entitled to. Who bequeathed it to them, if not the Exarchs? Now there's a question that's sure to haunt the Seers.<br /> <br /> *Yeah, yeah, I know the Oracles aren't really brought up in 2e. I admit, the analogy isn't perfect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T16:49:47-07:00","id":950795,"title":"","content":"What is a prison without its snitches and wardens?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T19:41:51-07:00","id":950871,"title":"","content":"Guardians are frequently portrayed as the Mage secret police, but on top of keeping watch over the Bound that's also a function of the Seers. It might be interesting to portray that in an area where the Seers have enough sway, the Guardians taking a character aside for a little chat and saying something along the lines of, &quot;Look, you think we're a pain in the ass because we stopped you from doing that? Just be glad it was us, and not -them-.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T19:52:13-07:00","id":950878,"title":"","content":"I always liked the idea that many Seers come from a really mundane place of just craving and greed and ignorance. Play up the wealth and temporal power aspect. Imagine a newly Awakened person who gets a private meeting, a la Mr. Anderson with Agent Smith: &quot;Hey, congrats on Awakening. We're the guys in charge. We'll take care of all of you and your family's bills and loans and medical debt and teach you how to use magic. You start Monday.&quot;<br /> <br /> Why would they present it as a real choice between Pentacle and Seers? Why tell the truth up front? Joining the Seers should feel like &quot;oh boy, I can get a job I love where I get to use the new magic powers I've been given!&quot; A potential Seer recruit should be thinking about joining the Pentacle in the way that a new hire at a law firm thinks about quitting their job, selling all their possessions, shaving their head and joining a monastery on the other side of the world. I guess you COULD, but you wouldn't seriously consider it.<br /> <br /> Joining the Seers is the reasonable choice. It's what your parents would have wanted.<br /> <br /> E: along with the Matrix thing, the Stephen King short story &quot;Everything's Eventual&quot; would be a really good model for this aspect of the Seers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 08-15-2016, 10:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T20:42:34-07:00","id":950888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/950771-seers-as-written?p=950878#post950878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always liked the idea that many Seers come from a really mundane place of just craving and greed and ignorance. Play up the wealth and temporal power aspect. Imagine a newly Awakened person who gets a private meeting, a la Mr. Anderson with Agent Smith: &quot;Hey, congrats on Awakening. We're the guys in charge. We'll take care of all of you and your family's bills and loans and medical debt and teach you how to use magic. You start Monday.&quot;<br /> <br /> Why would they present it as a real choice between Pentacle and Seers? Why tell the truth up front? Joining the Seers should feel like &quot;oh boy, I can get a job I love where I get to use the new magic powers I've been given!&quot; A potential Seer recruit should be thinking about joining the Pentacle in the way that a new hire at a law firm thinks about quitting their job, selling all their possessions, shaving their head and joining a monastery on the other side of the world. I guess you COULD, but you wouldn't seriously consider it.<br /> <br /> Joining the Seers is the reasonable choice. It's what your parents would have wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually ran that Mr. Anderson scene. Old world Syndcate to a newbie VA. Basically said Congratz on waking up, The world is broken because mankind is broken. Evil lurks in the heart of man. And we're only &quot;winning&quot; because we offered rationalism and use their own tools. You want to make the world a better place? Nothing's stopping yeah cept reality. So if you'd so kindly never get arrested again that would help me out a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T22:07:57-07:00","id":950925,"title":"","content":"Here's one of the ways I picture the seers, though of course it's a big group with a lot of different ways of doing things.<br /> <br /> Picture an X-files type scenario where aliens (the Exarchs) exist and are interacting with the world in secret. The seers are the ones on the inside of the conspiracy who communicate with the aliens and make secret deals on behalf of themselves and mankind. Yes, they have to keep a lot of secrets from the population at large although those are secrets that they're probably not ready for. They might occasionally have to do some morally questionable activities. However they keep the aliens happy enough to let their human agents handle things for them and that lets the conspirators run things here on Earth. Some of them like the way that puts them in charge of the world, some of them like the fringe benefits and some of them like the way they can help people by running a kinder system than the aliens would if they were directly running things. Because of their work there's no alien invasion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T22:39:46-07:00","id":950933,"title":"","content":"So I'm in the middle of running a Mage game and one of the two Mages joined the Seers. Both were brand-new Awakenings. They lived and worked in the part of the city controlled by the Seers, at one point trip their detection magicks, and a Seer Headhunter shows up at one of their doors and invited them both to dinner. Fancy place. Amazing food. <br /> <br /> Gives them a pretty standard Seer pitch. &quot;Hey the Exarchs blah blah basically any mortal needs - shelter, money, can be taken care of not because we are hyper-generous but because covering rent isn't exactly hard when you've got a guy on your team who can just make precious metals. You'll be asked to do things you don't want to do, just like every other job in the world.&quot; So on and so forth.<br /> <br /> One of the Mages was a professors of physics or some such at NYU and awoke as an Obrimos, was kinda reeling from the whole &quot;what just happened to physics oh god oh god&quot; thing. Asked what his job would be, basically got told that if he wanted to just research magic and do some light Indiana Jones work (and all other assigned duties) that would be fine. He just wouldn't get to go check out the most interesting stuff because, hey, seniority right?<br /> <br /> Guy jumped at the chance. Some day I'll run a Seer game and follow him down that rabbit hole and push him up against the dark side of that choice, but...let's be real. The picture in the book isn't the sales pitch unless their target has some shockingly specific tastes. That's for later.<br /> <br /> <br /> Because it's not just the whole &quot;everyone think they would be the hero but in reality very few people can manage it&quot; business. Its not just the bystander complex. Study after study shows that the more money you have (once you achieve &quot;true&quot; wealth) the most disconnected you become from others. And this isn't just money - it's MAGIC. it's EVERYTHING. you're so far above the 1% they look like those kids on TV you get asked to support for 10 cents a day. So yeah. You'll get jaded. You'll want more. And pretty soon you too Will be wearing an opera mask while doing lines off of the dying body of a crucified guy dressed up as Jesus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T03:25:33-07:00","id":951020,"title":"","content":"Without the Exarchs, the world in which we live cannot exist. It is -their- design, crafted to keep Humanity safe and secure.<br /> The Seers recognise this and work to protect the world that they've always known. Some do it for power, some for gratification, others still do it for the people they love and a few even believe that what they're doing is truly right.<br /> <br /> The Pentacle claims that the Exarchs are the symbols of tyranny, but in truth they are symbols of control. Someone needs to be in control after all, if not the Exarchs then who? What fills the power vacuum? An inscrutable machine with little regard for Humanity, monstrous Old Gods or perhaps new Exarchs to replace the old?<br /> No matter what follows, the world as we know it is over.<br /> <br /> The Seers -like- this world, flawed as it is. They don't want to lose their families or the lives they have made for themselves. They see the value in the status quo, which so many others seem blind to.<br /> Sure the Exarchs sometimes ask horrible things of them, but every atrocity serves to keep their world -alive-.<br /> ----------<br /> These are my thoughts on what might motivate someone to become a Seer, or perhaps what they might use to justify their actions. Obviously not every Seer thinks like this and I'd say many Lesser Ministries aren't even content with the status quo of the Archgenitors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksi plays Peek-a-boo for keeps. ~ nalak42","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/203-kleptomania","name":"Kleptomania","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T08:19:20-07:00","id":951117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/950771-seers-as-written?p=950791#post950791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b> <u>1</u> </b>Did they, though? Or was it just a handout from those upstart Oracles? //<u><b> 2 </b></u>Who bequeathed it to them, if not the Exarchs? Now there's a question that's sure to haunt the Seers.</div> </div> </div> </div>1 Yeah, Oracles are not really discussed, but i like the &quot;old&quot; terminology anyway; let's assume them and its role. One could say that they are just another Exarchs class nonetheless, which ties that to part 2. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T11:17:04-07:00","id":951211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/950771-seers-as-written?p=950773#post950773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As someone who's always struggled with faith, the idea of achieving Prelacy and having communication with the closest thing the Fallen World has to gods is a potent motivation.<br /> <br /> Beyond that, there's the sheer scale of the threat the Exarchs pose; they won so hard the timeline was forever changed, and trying to struggle against incarnate symbols of oppression is so unthinkably beyond the scope of possibility that it seems hopeless. Why not join the winning team and benefit from it? Why try to change the world if no one's managed a single measurable victory against them ever?</div> </div> </div> </div>Faith is a motive that doesn't get enough love. I've been monkeying with the role of Supernal sympathy in my games and it's brought faith front and center in a big way. Faith is what binds the Diamond together; what gives the Pentacle its purpose. Faith is strength and hope that defies the seemingly inevitable.<br /> <br /> Worth adding that a part of the Seer faith <i>is</i> the belief that that Exarchs are Atlantean sorcerers, though. Just like the story of Atlantis, it's a self-explaining myth they use to justify themselves. The Seers don't know that their gods are what they believe they are; it's just a trapping they dress in.<br /> <br /> From my personal experiences, the Seers are tricky to use. There's a natural temptation to make both sides of the holy war try to kill the other on-sight or instantly antagonistic to one another. This is chiefly due to a sense of dehumanization; that the other side is just looking for an opportunity to kill them too, and thus should be taken out as fast as possible. This isn't just a problem for STs but with players too; they're tense and fearful and often worrying about what the best way is to kill the Seer without a Wisdom drop.<br /> <br /> The best way to counter it, in my experience, is to make collaboration an expected part of the setting; something you have examples of. The one time I've ever successfully used the Seers in a way that didn't make them instant villain fodder, it was by making them slightly dodgy allies. This is pretty easy to do; just create a few Seer NPCs that everyone knows and does business with. In my case, it was a Thyrsus called the King of Rats, who spied on much of New York in the 70s. He was frequently a source of information, usually in exchange for money or rotes, and occasionally an ally when the Pentacle needed to battle the fire spirits eating the Bronx or the local werewolves. Same went for any scelesti or reapers in the area.<br /> <br /> The Rat, as he was more affectionately known, was a surprisingly good ally; he kept his word on any matter of import and frequently provided good intel. It just meant that any service you drew from him meant you were aiding in his plan to keep the Bronx mired in ruin and decay. He used his powers to control rat spirits and was revered as a prophet by a number of Rat Host communities. Delving into New York's sewers without the Rat's permission was suicide and the sewer worker's union was basically a cult feeding his power because any sewer workers who <i>didn't</i> offer the Rat his due disappeared.<br /> <br /> Not someone you feel good about working with, but far from the worst ally you could have. At least he's not a Tremere, right?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T17:15:31-07:00","id":951391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/950771-seers-as-written?p=951211#post951211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Faith is a motive that doesn't get enough love. I've been monkeying with the role of Supernal sympathy in my games and it's brought faith front and center in a big way. Faith is what binds the Diamond together; what gives the Pentacle its purpose. Faith is strength and hope that defies the seemingly inevitable.<br /> <br /> Worth adding that a part of the Seer faith <i>is</i> the belief that that Exarchs are Atlantean sorcerers, though. Just like the story of Atlantis, it's a self-explaining myth they use to justify themselves. The Seers don't know that their gods are what they believe they are; it's just a trapping they dress in.<br /> <br /> From my personal experiences, the Seers are tricky to use. There's a natural temptation to make both sides of the holy war try to kill the other on-sight or instantly antagonistic to one another. This is chiefly due to a sense of dehumanization; that the other side is just looking for an opportunity to kill them too, and thus should be taken out as fast as possible. This isn't just a problem for STs but with players too; they're tense and fearful and often worrying about what the best way is to kill the Seer without a Wisdom drop.<br /> <br /> The best way to counter it, in my experience, is to make collaboration an expected part of the setting; something you have examples of. The one time I've ever successfully used the Seers in a way that didn't make them instant villain fodder, it was by making them slightly dodgy allies. This is pretty easy to do; just create a few Seer NPCs that everyone knows and does business with. In my case, it was a Thyrsus called the King of Rats, who spied on much of New York in the 70s. He was frequently a source of information, usually in exchange for money or rotes, and occasionally an ally when the Pentacle needed to battle the fire spirits eating the Bronx or the local werewolves. Same went for any scelesti or reapers in the area.<br /> <br /> The Rat, as he was more affectionately known, was a surprisingly good ally; he kept his word on any matter of import and frequently provided good intel. It just meant that any service you drew from him meant you were aiding in his plan to keep the Bronx mired in ruin and decay. He used his powers to control rat spirits and was revered as a prophet by a number of Rat Host communities. Delving into New York's sewers without the Rat's permission was suicide and the sewer worker's union was basically a cult feeding his power because any sewer workers who <i>didn't</i> offer the Rat his due disappeared.<br /> <br /> Not someone you feel good about working with, but far from the worst ally you could have. At least he's not a Tremere, right?</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/236x/c8/ec/94/c8ec944dd4c79efcbc623c31748e6871.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> [[warning I will not be able to spell anything well today]]<br /> <br /> Thats actually a pretty cool concept. Something a lot of people don't get is that you don't just wake up and decide to be evil moustache evil. Everyone is the hero of their own story. The idea of pure satistic is too much of a narrative crutch. And it's been very frustrating trying to get players to see when the bad guy sometimes has a point. Online/Offline being different beasts. It's So easy for people to Demonize, because it plays off two very power emotions fear and anger. It's really easy to make a good hero; It's really hard to make a good villian. It's the Forest in the Trees argument and it takes away identity from characters when you lump them all of a certain faction as the base line. and one of the reasons I find the polical season so nonsencial.<br /> <br /> Some people don't want their ideas challenged and thats not always a good thing. never challenging your ideas leads to stagnation and weakness. If you can't defend your own points in opposition, how pragmatic and benifical are they? This is actually scientifically kind of proven. the more questions we answer, the more questions those answer spawn. And if I may, it is no conicidence that the word question, includes Quest. The Hero's journey The Hero's quest is about the unknown working wreasling and coming to a conclusion. Then bringing the unknown into the known. Bringing the dark into the light.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://static.tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pub/images/heros_journey4_8462.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Minor Note The Inital Refusal is a very important part of the arc but seldom illustrated.<br /> <br /> The setting I like to toy around with are the war by proxies. Nameless / Lesser known / Local Factions. Vying for influence and power in an area. Its lets the players more or less see a gradient of dedication. Where each side was patronizing a faction under the table. Members that show a lot of potiental and dedication become recruitment targets for the larger factions. A sliding slope. And then the larger &quot;war&quot; becomes a more centered part of the narrative. and the innerfaction conflicts and relations evole naturally.<br /> <br /> &quot;Should you do that thing? No don't do that thing, do this thing. Guys if we don't do X, Y will happen. Y is only a theory and not worth looking into. We need to go on the offensive! No build up our forts for winter!&quot;<br /> <br /> The main factions offer to the players reward safety and pay for services rendered like a real organization. Say all you want about altruism but at the end of the day. Those R.O.U.S in the Basement aren't killing themselves. Bills need to be paid, Watches need to be manned, and a meandering P.I. needs to strap together a Harpon Zipline from stuff lying around the attic. <br /> <br /> I often like playing the unalign just so I can work with different factions without the overhead, and so the character's decisions are more of a moral / survival alignment rather than an idealogical one. Knights were just hired muscle that got romanticed later in the telling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Placeholder","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11731-mercset","name":"MercSet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11731_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"277"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T22:35:43-07:00","id":952324,"title":"","content":"I think the best way to humanize the Seers and still keep them canon is by making its lower level members mundane people. They don't get or care about the ideologies that drive their organization but instead are just focused on getting the payment they were promised from their bosses. In essence, most Seers should be more concerned about putting their kids through an ivy school or getting their parents into the best old folks in the country than enjoying actively oppressing mankind and keeping the human race ignorant and small.<br /> <br /> They're still selfish, to be sure, but I think this interpretation makes them more human and relatable than a Diamond mage's ancient high-minded ideals.<br /> <br /> Remember, the banality of evil is far more interesting and real than Chaotic Evil.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T01:54:43-07:00","id":953051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/950771-seers-as-written?p=950781#post950781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing. they were just born into it. And don't even get me started on those socialist Libertines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just remember that nobody is really &quot;born&quot; into magic. This ain't Harry Potter, and Awakening isn't a superhero origin, but a process that a person undertakes through their own will. You may be more likely to Awaken if your parents were, but that's because being surrounded by magical strangeness spurs Awakenings generally.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T06:46:58-07:00","id":953133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/950771-seers-as-written?p=953051#post953051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just remember that nobody is really &amp;quot;born&amp;quot; into magic. This ain't Harry Potter, and Awakening isn't a superhero origin, but a process that a person undertakes through their own will. You may be more likely to Awaken if your parents were, but that's because being surrounded by magical strangeness spurs Awakenings generally.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know they aren't literally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T07:31:57-07:00","id":953156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weirdboyz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/950771-seers-as-written?p=952324#post952324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the best way to humanize the Seers and still keep them canon is by making its lower level members mundane people. They don't get or care about the ideologies that drive their organization but instead are just focused on getting the payment they were promised from their bosses. In essence, most Seers should be more concerned about putting their kids through an ivy school or getting their parents into the best old folks in the country than enjoying actively oppressing mankind and keeping the human race ignorant and small.<br /> <br /> They're still selfish, to be sure, but I think this interpretation makes them more human and relatable than a Diamond mage's ancient high-minded ideals.<br /> <br /> Remember, the banality of evil is far more interesting and real than Chaotic Evil.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, they're basically the bit workers at things like a foreclosure department, or telemarketing farm? Yeah, it's a crappy job that leads to human misery, but someone's gotta do and you have bills to pay, right? <hr /><br /> I had the idea for a kind of departmental exile Seer. They were really talented at bindings and wardings, and transferred to the area by superiors to keep a lid on Bound in the region. They don't really cop fully to the party line, though, and they pretty much fail at politics, but they are <i>really</i> good at wards. They basically became a victim of their own success, and have had support and allies slowly leeched away over the years to other interests (there isn't anything else of interest in the area, other than the Bound that need to keep sealed), until they are the only one left holding down the fort. Basically, the concept/archetype of the crotchety old man forgotten in the tail end of nowhere. Local Nameless and Pentacle Mages find them more amusing than anything - no one wants to (or possibly <i>could</i>) keep up the duty of making sure the Bound stay locked up, and the Seer is too busy doing that to really oppress anyone (even if they were inclined to).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-18-2016, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T09:05:14-07:00","id":953220,"title":"","content":"Essentially all of the Exarch Tyrranies are extremes of systems that <i>can</i> be quite beneficial. The right person at the right place in time can bring out wonders. People <i>do</i> tend to behave better when they know people are watching. These aspects are not entirely removed from the Exarch hierarchies and a person could easily cling to such a thing as a rationale for why what they are doing is ultimately good. Throw in the &quot;cosmic reality needs this order&quot; aspect as a more esoteric thing, and you've got the makings of a Seer Pylon that tries to do good by containing humanity and their excesses.<br /> <br /> Remember that 1e example FC character who was bullied and now runs surveillance 24/7? He'd make an easy recruit to the Panopticon if he's not actually a plant sent to recruit. He makes their case for them in his write-up. (One of the <i>Legacies</i> books, IIRC.)<br /> <br /> Religion does good things for people and many seers could actively apply themselves to setting up those systems. Their need to control these things could be the corrupting influence. The corruption of the good works by the emphasis on doing good works as a group leading to needing the group to continue so it can do good works happens a lot. Some Seers could actively fight such trends, assuming that was their Exarch's actual intent. Don't forget the Pyramid includes members. Those fighting for power and such make dead-end philosophies to trap their subordinates and so on. That's as written. It's not a huge leap to picture that some of these gain supernal support from other ideals.<br /> <br /> The original organization might even have coalesces around the noble ideal but the corrupt form subverted and won control. As below, and all that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Personally, I like the idea that the Free Council is a pyramid of an Exarch of the Tyranny of the Masses... or becoming one. A mystery cult (who'd be declared left-handed were they ever exposed) within them overtly worships their patron Exarch though many of the rank and file worship her in the name of Democracy. A silver lining approach could be that there is an Oracle up there that some others are worshiping, but that could all be spin.<br /> <br /> <br /> People are their most tyrannical when they assume that they would do better because they <i>are</i> better. &quot;If only I had the power...&quot; is exceedingly common. <br /> <br /> Take any movement and consider their worst aspects. Simply figure out a mindset that can justify that and you have a Seer. Some could justify it as a cost for the good being done. (&quot;at least they're raising awareness&quot; or &quot;Sometimes, you break some eggs.&quot;) Others would justify it as balance against oppressors. (&quot;They earned this.&quot;) Some would simply not accept that something is a problem in the first place. (&quot;Sure we do that, but how is that a problem?&quot;)<br /> <br /> Someone who feels slighted and oppressed will gravitate to any Exarch who appears to provide the power they crave.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T09:29:55-07:00","id":953241,"title":"","content":"Problem being that Prelates are usually in charge and fully aware of the Exarch's intentions of corrupting potentially good things into systems of oppression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T10:51:49-07:00","id":953287,"title":"","content":"Prelates are in charge of the true hierarchies as defined by the top being the Exarch, and their voices being the masters and archmastes, yes. That bit about false hierarchies, though? There must be latitude from the middle levels on down or those sidetrack hierarchies wouldn't fool very many people.<br /> <br /> Even the prelates, though, don't have to be simply doing evil because they enjoy it or have blind faith. A focusing of the same principle applies: the prelate can believe that the Exarch is a force for good in the world because it destroys some hated thing. A Praetorian might consider the horrors of war a lesson to the world, a punishment levied against the evils humanity keeps committing, or even fall into the mindset of Marvel's Apocalypse. The first might be perverting attempts to limit dehumanized combat because that would allow people to miss the lesson. The punished shouldn't escape the full horror.<br /> <br /> Unless you posit comprehensible &amp; <i>human</i> Exarchs, you have plenty of room for multiple interpretations among anything below the merging phase. Possibly <i>still</i> there, as multiple faces of the thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T11:19:14-07:00","id":953305,"title":"","content":"That's a good way of putting it. I just didn't want the conversation to drift into the misconception that the Seers who do the most to shape the Pyramid aren't aware of what they're doing. Rationalizing it is fine, they must have to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T23:22:43-07:00","id":953691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/950771-seers-as-written?p=953133#post953133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know they aren't literally.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Please don't take it personally. It's just the #1 misconception people insert into the game so I like to address it when the opportunity arises.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-18T23:28:28-07:00","id":953692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/950771-seers-as-written?p=953287#post953287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prelates are in charge of the true hierarchies as defined by the top being the Exarch, and their voices being the masters and archmastes, yes. That bit about false hierarchies, though? There must be latitude from the middle levels on down or those sidetrack hierarchies wouldn't fool very many people.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're worthy, you *make* your branch relevant, even if your enemies route around it. The Seers proceed from the assumption that the Lie is what people deserve. If you Awaken and aren't a Seer, you *still* deserve it. If you're an incompetent Seer, maybe you deserve only partial release from the Lie. Payment requires effort. You must continually demonstrate your ability to earn access to the apparatus of the Throne and the Exarchs themselves, and must test people's worthiness constantly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T07:22:04-07:00","id":953821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/950771-seers-as-written?p=953691#post953691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please don't take it personally. It's just the #1 misconception people insert into the game so I like to address it when the opportunity arises.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I don't. Sorry if my post made it sound like I did. We're cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T21:30:04-07:00","id":954805,"title":"","content":"I've been mulling over how to play the seers as depraved but still believable villains and to try and understand how someone joins the seers also trying to come up with good plot hooks that show the Seers being predatory assholes.<br /> <br /> The chronicle I am running is in a small town with teenage sleepers who get closer and closer to the truth until they eventually awaken. The orders are absent from the chronicle as the local Mysterium cabal was wiped out 20 years prior to the story in spectacularly brutal fashion by the Seers who are also killed in the encounter, except for one survivor who returns to the town if the players get to noisy with their actions. The Seer villain who I haven't named yet was going to mind control his way into becoming their guidance counselor and try to screw them over or win them over, the later option involves them doing something truly evil to show their loyalty. I am thinking the players should encounter depraved things that the Seers did over the course of the game before he shows up too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1563-oriontyson","name":"OrionTyson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T23:50:33-07:00","id":954860,"title":"","content":"If the Seers do one thing that is depraved, and they do it on the regular, it's what they do to Sleepwalkers and Sleepers. Sleepwalkers get twisted into servitors, twisted half people with not a whole lot going for them and only more duties to perform for their Seer masters to look forward to. Sleepers get used as meat puppets, the Exarchs even provide artifacts to allow Seers to take possession of Sleepers whenever they want. I imagine that on top of possessing Sleepers so that Seers can operate magically by proxy they probably abuse the privilege as well forcing the Sleeper to do things they'd never do if they were in control of themselves so that the Seer can live on drugs, sex, violence or whatever vicariously through them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T12:02:39-07:00","id":955059,"title":"","content":"What stops you from doing that with Pentacle, though? Maybe it's a fatigue induced thought, but I feel that anything I could do with Seers as villains and antagonists, I could do with Pentacle, and do it better than if I used Seers instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T14:55:13-07:00","id":955203,"title":"","content":"Nothing, and I'm not fond of the idea of using too broad a brush when describing any group, but Seers are the ones given and readily deploying the artifacts that allow them to more easily commit those kinds of acts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T18:37:08-07:00","id":955344,"title":"","content":"I was trying to come up with other heinous acts that villains might commit but they need to be ones that are more lawful Evil than chaotic evil. The using people as Meat Puppets is a good one. Here's another idea that I had. I want to give seers who are mastigos more fun. So for instance, a Moors Seer my bond ghosts to be their slaves or Guardians. These being ghosts of people that they killed. Another was infiltrating institutions and sabotaging research with life magic. Or purging an entire area of access to the spirit world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1563,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1563-oriontyson","user":"OrionTyson","date":". 08-21-2016, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1563-oriontyson","name":"OrionTyson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1563_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}